[al:新概念英语第一册]
[ti:A Walk Through the Woods]
[00:01.08]Lesson 143 | 第143课
[00:03.50]A walk through the woods | 林中散步
[00:06.74]Listen to the tape then answer this question. | 听录音，然后回答这个问题。
[00:12.19]What was so funny about the words on the sign? | 牌子上的字有什么好笑的？
[00:18.64]I live in a very old town which is surrounded by beautiful woods. | 我住在一个非常古老的小镇，它被美丽的树林环绕着。
[00:27.78]It is a famous beauty spot. | 这是一个著名的风景区。
[00:31.42]On Sundays, hundreds of people come from the city to see our town and to walk through the woods. | 每到星期天，成百上千的人从城里赶来参观我们的小镇，并在树林中散步。
[00:41.64]Visitors have been asked to keep the woods clean and tidy. | 游客们被要求保持树林的清洁整齐。
[00:48.80]Litter baskets have been placed under the trees, but people still throw their rubbish everywhere. | 树下放置了垃圾筐，但人们仍然随处乱扔垃圾。
[00:58.43]Last Wednesday, I went for a walk in the woods. | 上个星期三，我到树林里散步。
[01:04.62]What I saw made me very sad. | 我看到的一切让我很难过。
[01:10.02]I counted seven old cars and three old refrigerators. | 我数出了七辆旧汽车和三台旧冰箱。
[01:17.84]The little baskets were empty and the ground was covered with pieces of paper, | 那些垃圾筐都是空的，地上却铺满了碎纸片，
[01:25.58]cigarette ends, old tyres, empty bottles and rusty tins. | 烟头、旧轮胎、空瓶子和生锈的罐头盒。
[01:34.42]Among the rubbish, I found a sign which said, 'Anyone who leaves litter in these woods will be prosecuted!' | 在这些垃圾中，我发现了一个牌子，上面写着：“凡在此树林中乱扔垃圾者，将受到起诉！”